ses the observer's exact address succeeds. This is a client-contract/documentation or API-behavior mismatch, not a demonstrated CFT safety or unbounded-liveness defect for a matching-address promotion. The evidence does not establish whether the API comment should be corrected or the target handling changed.\",\n \"answers\": {},\n \"knowledge\": [\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"7034811e609340afbfc17ad24f2fc632-knowledge-0\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"Promotion requires the observer's stored address; empty, invalid, or different targets do not follow the documented ignored-target path.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"entry_id\": \"c5b7c76791cb4a1da22e4fada40d9ed8-knowledge-0\",\n   \"revision\": 1,\n   \"assertion\": \"The control accepted only the matching address and retained the observer role for the rejected targets.\"\n  }\n ],\n \"counterevidence\": [\n  \"The matching-address control accepted the promotion and removed the observer role, so the operation is available with the stored address.\",\n  \"The source and existing test deliberately reject a different address, indicating the address-equality guard is intentional.\",\n  \"The control starts at the membership state machine and does not include the request-level validator, so it confirms code behavior rather than the full documented client path.\"\n ],\n \"limitations\": [\n  \"The control does not execute NodeHost RequestAddNode or a custom target validator.\",\n  \"It does not resolve whether the API comment or the membership guard is normative.\",\n  \"The mismatch is lower-severity client behavior; it does not establish a CFT safety or unbounded-liveness defect for a matching-address promotion.\",\n  \"No transport, persistence, restart, or concurrent membership transition was exercised.\"\n ],\n \"joint_history\": \"\",\n \"failure_attribution\": null,\n \"operation_id\": \"c5b7c76791cb4a1da22e4fada40d9ed8\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
