{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-18_14-39-49-dragonboat_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns = json.load(open('state.json'))\nrec = [v for v in s['interpretations'] if v['id'].startswith('c5b7c767')][0]\nkeep = ['investigation_id','experiment_id','source_ids','executions','conclusion','defect_claim','rationale','answers','knowledge','counterevidence','limitations','joint_history','failure_attribution']\nu = {k: rec[k] for k in keep if k in rec}\nu['knowledge'] = list(u['knowledge']) + [{\n  \\\"entry_id\\\": \\\"@addnode-target-validator\\\",\n  \\\"revision\\\": 1,\n  \\\"assertion\\\": \\\"The target validator that gates the ErrInvalidAddress branch is selected by the NodeHost configuration, so a permissive custom validator moves the rejection to the membership layer instead.\\\"\n}]\nlim = list(u['limitations'])\nlim[0] = \\\"The control does not execute NodeHost RequestAddNode; the request-level branch is traced from source, and only the default validator resolution (NodeHost ID mode, transport validator, or stringutil.IsValidAddress) is read, not exercised.\\\"\nu['limitations'] = lim\nout = {\n \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Pin down which validator produces the request-level ErrInvalidAddress branch. GetTargetValidator selects id.IsNodeHostID in AddressByNodeHostID mode, the transport factory's Validate when one is configured, and stringutil.IsValidAddress otherwise; requestConfigChange applies that predicate to every non-remove change before it builds the ConfigChange. So the documented ignored-target invocation is rejected at the request layer under the default validator and would instead reach the membership-layer rejection under a permissive custom validator. The control, conclusion and defect claim are unchanged.\\\",\n \\\"sources\\\": [\n  {\\\"id\\\": \\\"nodehost-target-validator\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"config/config.go\\\", \